# The repo-root build context is used by iris/Dockerfile
# (docker-context: . in iris_build-and-push-docker.yml).
# Whitelist exactly what that Dockerfile COPYs so the context stays small
# and untracked local files never get uploaded to the builder.
#
# A Dockerfile added here without its inputs whitelisted fails with
# "failed to compute cache key: … not found" — the path is simply absent from
# the context.
*
# The session image installs the repository's own hook environments at build
# time, because a session has no network to install them with. Every config:
# the root one delegates to the services through sub-pre-commit, and they pin
# their own versions of the same tools.
!.pre-commit-config.yaml
!iris/.pre-commit-config.yaml
!athena/.pre-commit-config.yaml
!iris/pyproject.toml
!iris/poetry.lock
!iris/src/iris
!iris/log_conf.yml
!iris/models
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
